{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles","id":1443873,"title":"Practitioners of the Invisible Arts (Cultist Simulator in Chronicles)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-14T07:01:16-07:00","id":1443873,"title":"Practitioners of the Invisible Arts (Cultist Simulator in Chronicles)","content":"So, due to a complex series of circumstances I ended up basically writing up mechanics for playing a character from the Weather Factory game <a href=\"https://store.steampowered.com/app/718670/Cultist_Simulator/\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Cultist Simulator</i></a> in Chronicles of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Now, I know we have more than enough cultists around these parts, but if nothing else <i>Cultist Simulator</i> has a strong atmosphere and thematics to it. Characters begin as something closest to mortal occultists, but through dedication to the secret Principles of the world, and exploration of the Mansus - sometimes called the House of the Sun - which stands in dreams and perhaps service to the Hours, the secret gods which dwell there, they can become rather more than merely mortal.<br /> <br /> The core of the thing is playable, but I need ideas for Merits and rituals to flesh it out more, as well as general second opinions on mechanics. I'm more than happy to discuss it here or in the CultSim Discord, and to field ideas.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you're at all interested, please take a look at the document linked <b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LezZSGk7LAENYbjchhkgsdmCi-iLIk6M3lfeC4eUrog/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">here</a></b>, and leave comments or posts on the thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 04-14-2021, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T20:00:46-07:00","id":1443974,"title":"","content":"I WANTED TO DO THIS TOO DAM-<br /> <br /> Just kidding, of course. I probably couldn\u2019t have done it well enough, since I never actually played the game. But the lore, oooh...<br /> <br /> Anyways, will read once I get back to my laptop.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Secret Histories is curiously missing. Why?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 04-15-2021, 01:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T01:08:48-07:00","id":1444001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1443974#post1443974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I WANTED TO DO THIS TOO DAM-<br /> <br /> Just kidding, of course. I probably couldn\u2019t have done it well enough, since I never actually played the game. But the lore, oooh...<br /> <br /> Anyways, will read once I get back to my laptop.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Secret Histories is curiously missing. Why?</div> </div> </div> </div>Secret Histories isn't really a power in itself. It's 'just' knowledge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T01:19:20-07:00","id":1444003,"title":"","content":"True, but if the Principles can substitute for Skills, I thought it could still have a use. <br /> <br /> <br /> More questions: What would a Hallow look like? Maybe the Burgeoning Corpse could have some healing ability to reflect the Phyraxian aspect? Any \u2018official\u2019 stance on how this fits with the wider CofD cosmologies, especially with Ritual Sorcerers and the Astral?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T02:10:06-07:00","id":1444004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1444003#post1444003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but if the Principles can substitute for Skills, I thought it could still have a use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. On one hand, I can see your point there, but on the other if it doesn't have magical Merits and the like, I can only really see Secret Histories as a 'dump Principle', as it were.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1444003#post1444003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More questions: What would a Hallow look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>It very much depends on what kind of Influence the Hallow produces. A Hallow of Knock is probably a building where doors don't work right, or open into places they shouldn't, or which is inhabited by a Younger Sister. Meanwhile a Moth-Hallow is a place of whimsy and woods and at least a little bit of madness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1444003#post1444003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe the Burgeoning Corpse could have some healing ability to reflect the Phyraxian aspect?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have been wondering about how that could potentially be implemented. Going by the description of its Phylaxian ability:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I will place a lock of hair in the hollow of this one's chest, and with luck, one day, the sickness will seek me there instead. </div> </div> </div>It seems to be less of a 'do this to cure a disease' thing and more a preventative measure, of sorts. That said, diseases are generally less central/vital in CofD compared to the Cultist Simulator game. So I'm not entirely sure how to handle it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1444003#post1444003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any \u2018official\u2019 stance on how this fits with the wider CofD cosmologies, especially with Ritual Sorcerers and the Astral?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, you <i>could</i> handle it by just adding the Mansus to the existing CofD cosmology, but my personal approach would essentially be to substitute the Mansus for the Astral, and to remove the Underworld. The dead, if they linger, do so on Earth or pass into the House of the Sun, where they may linger, or pass the White Door to become Voiceless and rest amidst the Orchard of Lights, or make the Ascent of Knives into the service of the Sun-in-Rags. I think spirits are pretty compatible with a CultSim game - You'd probably want Lantern to see things in Twilight and Knock to breach the Gauntlet - but in general this isn't really something I'd want to run as a crossover with any of the major gamelines.<br /> <br /> Regarding ritual sorcerers, I've been considering that, and I do somewhat like the idea that practitioners are natural ritual sorcerers, and can substitute Influences for Pillar points to some extent. On the other hand, it might be easier to just have a lot of closed rites have equivalents in rituals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 04-15-2021, 05:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T03:29:58-07:00","id":1444008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1444004#post1444004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. On one hand, I can see your point there, but on the other if it doesn't have magical Merits and the like, I can only really see Secret Histories as a 'dump Principle', as it were.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Dump Stats should be avoided. Hmm... maybe it should be nipped after all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It very much depends on what kind of Influence the Hallow produces. A Hallow of Knock is probably a building where doors don't work right, or open into places they shouldn't, or which is inhabited by a Younger Sister. Meanwhile a Moth-Hallow is a place of whimsy and woods and at least a little bit of madness. </div> </div> </div>Good to know. Kinda was wondering, since AFAIK Cultist Simulator didn't have things like Hallows.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> I have been wondering about how that could potentially be implemented. Going by the description of its Phylaxian ability:<br /> <br /> It seems to be less of a 'do this to cure a disease' thing and more a preventative measure, of sorts. That said, diseases are generally less central/vital in CofD compared to the Cultist Simulator game. So I'm not entirely sure how to handle it. </div> </div> </div>Maybe something like the Shared Fate spell, where the wound/ailment just... happens on the deflected effigy or something. The other spirits have even weirder descriptions for that ability but the same effect, so there's less need to match the flavor and mech. <br /> <br /> Or maybe just add &quot;Treating wounds and diseases&quot; as one of its Best At actions? I'd imagine it's not something widely known even among these occultists. Who'd even think about it!<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> So, you <i>could</i> handle it by just adding the Mansus to the existing CofD cosmology, but my personal approach would essentially be to substitute the Mansus for the Astral, and to remove the Underworld. The dead, if they linger, do so on Earth or pass into the House of the Sun, where they may linger, or pass the White Door to become Voiceless and rest amidst the Orchard of Lights, or make the Ascent of Knives into the service of the Sun-in-Rags. I think spirits are pretty compatible with a CultSim game - You'd probably want Lantern to see things in Twilight and Knock to breach the Gauntlet - but in general this isn't really something I'd want to run as a crossover with any of the major gamelines. </div> </div> </div><br /> Oooh, that sounds nice. And avoiding crossover is fine too, though I'll probably spin it differently. But that's just me.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Regarding ritual sorcerers, I've been considering that, and I do somewhat like the idea that practitioners are natural ritual sorcerers, and can substitute Influences for Pillar points to some extent. On the other hand, it might be easier to just have a lot of closed rites have equivalents in rituals. </div> </div> </div>Influences as Pillar points actually makes a lot of sense; Sekhem is life energy, with &quot;life&quot; in the sense of experiences lived and emotions felt, right? Sounds like Influences!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T03:48:11-07:00","id":1444010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1444008#post1444008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good to know. Kinda was wondering, since AFAIK Cultist Simulator didn't have things like Hallows.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't, no, but I wanted a way for PCs to have a reasonably reliable source of low-level Influences without having to dream-quest for everything.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1444008#post1444008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe something like the Shared Fate spell, where the wound/ailment just... happens on the deflected effigy or something. The other spirits have even weirder descriptions for that ability but the same effect, so there's less need to match the flavor and mech.<br /> <br /> Or maybe just add &quot;Treating wounds and diseases&quot; as one of its Best At actions? I'd imagine it's not something widely known even among these occultists. Who'd even think about it!</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter does seem like a pretty good way to cut the Gordian knot. Though I might add something in there like 'Putting a lock of hair in its chest allows it to ignore the need for medical tools when treating you'.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1444008#post1444008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oooh, that sounds nice. And avoiding crossover is fine too, though I'll probably spin it differently. But that's just me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind if I ask how you might spin it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1444008#post1444008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Influences as Pillar points actually makes a lot of sense; Sekhem is life energy, with &quot;life&quot; in the sense of experiences lived and emotions felt, right? Sounds like Influences!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll probably add a sidebar to that effect, then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T04:10:12-07:00","id":1444011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1444004#post1444004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. On one hand, I can see your point there, but on the other if it doesn't have magical Merits and the like, I can only really see Secret Histories as a 'dump Principle', as it were.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it doesn't fit the structure of the other Principles and risk becoming a dump stat, maybe it's better to change how it is gained so that you can get dots in it without having to spend from the limited dots gained from Insight? I was thinking it could be a 1-5 dot Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T04:12:03-07:00","id":1444012,"title":"","content":"One thing I'm debating adding to the thing is the ability to 'subvert' Influences like in the game - that is, take an Influence of one type and transform it into one of another, in a specific 'cycle' (Moth -&gt; Lantern -&gt; Forge -&gt; Edge -&gt; Winter -&gt; Heart -&gt; Grail -&gt; Moth, and any can be subverted to Knock). I'm not sure whether or not I should, though.<br /> <br /> From a functional standpoint subversion exists in the original mostly as a way to counter RNGsus being a bitch sometimes, but in a tabletop game A) you're not at the whim of RNG when it comes to what Influences you find and B) you're going to be playing with others, or at the very least with NPCs, and in those circumstances I was thinking it might be more interesting to have influences be non-fungible, but rather serving as a form of currency between practitioners. Say you happen across a Forge Influence, but you only know Grail magic. You can trade that Influence to a friend or acquaintance for help, or an Influence of theirs and so on.<br /> <br /> The other reason I'm a little reluctant to include it is <br /> <br /> On the other hand, there is still a certain element of 'I might need X while I have Y', or 'I have a source of X but I want Y', and subversion gives you a way to address those problems. Plus, I like the way that the ability to subvert one Influence into another implies that these things aren't totally separate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T04:21:45-07:00","id":1444014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1444011#post1444011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it doesn't fit the structure of the other Principles and risk becoming a dump stat, maybe it's better to change how it is gained so that you can get dots in it without having to spend from the limited dots gained from Insight? I was thinking it could be a 1-5 dot Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>What would the Merit do? In the game, Secret Histories just represents knowledge of places of power or, well, the Histories. And I think that's better handled in CofD as just Occult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T04:24:49-07:00","id":1444015,"title":"","content":"I <i>really</i> like this. I like it a lot!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1444004#post1444004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, you <i>could</i> handle it by just adding the Mansus to the existing CofD cosmology, but my personal approach would essentially be to substitute the Mansus for the Astral, and to remove the Underworld. The dead, if they linger, do so on Earth or pass into the House of the Sun, where they may linger, or pass the White Door to become Voiceless and rest amidst the Orchard of Lights, or make the Ascent of Knives into the service of the Sun-in-Rags. I think spirits are pretty compatible with a CultSim game - You'd probably want Lantern to see things in Twilight and Knock to breach the Gauntlet - but in general this isn't really something I'd want to run as a crossover with any of the major gamelines.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t mind. Though it <i>would</i> be interesting to see the stereotypes on these fellows that more \u2018normal\u2019 Occultists, Hunters and the various varieties of Supernaturals (be they Major (I.e. Werewolves), Minor (E.g. Ghouls) or Merit (Such as Stigmatics)) would hold, and vice versa. If I was a betting man (which I ain\u2019t), I\u2019d be putting my money that the various Major Supernaturals would have Stereotypes that could be summed up as a mixture of sheer WTF?!?!?!?!?! type confusion, and yellow-soiling levels of terror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T04:33:30-07:00","id":1444016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerrorCooper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1444015#post1444015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <i>really</i> like this. I like it a lot!<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t mind. Though it <i>would</i> be interesting to see the stereotypes on these fellows that more \u2018normal\u2019 Occultists, Hunters and the various varieties of Supernaturals (be they Major (I.e. Werewolves), Minor (E.g. Ghouls) or Merit (Such as Stigmatics)) would hold, and vice versa. If I was a betting man (which I ain\u2019t), I\u2019d be putting my money that the various Major Supernaturals would have Stereotypes that could be summed up as a mixture of sheer WTF?!?!?!?!?! type confusion, and yellow-soiling levels of terror.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be interesting. And depending on what Principles a given practitioner favors, they could certainly have interesting interactions with different supernatural types. For instance, vampirism and Grail have a lot in common, Moth lends itself to wild places and shapeshifting, and I wouldn't be surprised if werewolves and Moth-practitioners have a tendency to run into one another, while Knock lets you get into all <i>kinds </i>of interesting places you probably shouldn't be. Lantern and mages' obsessions probably result in them running into each other as well.<br /> <br /> Apart from all that, you could potentially situate the Mansus as some kind of special location within the Astral, though that runs the risk of lessening the Hours to 'mere' extremely-powerful goetia.<br /> <br /> And then there's the Worms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T04:51:23-07:00","id":1444018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1444016#post1444016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be interesting. And depending on what Principles a given practitioner favors, they could certainly have interesting interactions with different supernatural types. For instance, vampirism and Grail have a lot in common, Moth lends itself to wild places and shapeshifting, and I wouldn't be surprised if werewolves and Moth-practitioners have a tendency to run into one another, while Knock lets you get into all <i>kinds</i> of interesting places you probably shouldn't be. Lantern and mages' obsessions probably result in them running into each other as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>And considering the fact that any and all practitioner of the Invisible Arts with a sufficient amount of Insight can have an affinity with up to six different Principles, they\u2019d probably be able to actively mind-screw other supernaturals, <i>and maybe even successfully get away with it!</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1444016#post1444016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apart from all that, you could potentially situate the Mansus as some kind of special location within the Astral, though that runs the risk of lessening the Hours to 'mere' extremely-powerful goetia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and that does <b><i>NOT</i></b> do them proper justice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1444016#post1444016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then there's the Worms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah... *shudders*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T05:00:46-07:00","id":1444019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerrorCooper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1444018#post1444018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And considering the fact that any and all practitioner of the Invisible Arts with a sufficient amount of Insight can have an affinity with up to six different Principles, they\u2019d probably be able to actively mind-screw other supernaturals, <i>and maybe even successfully get away with it!</i></div> </div> </div> </div>One thing about practitioners is that they aren't able to directly raise their traits above 5, but within the purview of their Principles they can get very scary quite quickly. An Edge-adept is likely to be quite the terrifying fighter, even before you add in Merits like Coat of Scars, for instance. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerrorCooper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1444018#post1444018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, and that does <b><i>NOT</i></b> do them proper justice.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was basically my rationale for replacing the Astral, though you could potentially treat the Hours as beings not unlike the Aeons - beings that reside in the Astral but aren't <i>from humanity</i>, or even really from the world like the inhabitants of the Anima Mundi. In fact, you could potentially do something like situate the Wood and the Mansus at the 'heart' of the Astral - a point where the Glory (which, let's face it, has some big Supernal vibes) emanates into a kind of 'tree of life', and all the rest of the Astral is just the muddle that happens outside the Wood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerrorCooper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1444018#post1444018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah... *shudders*</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T05:24:09-07:00","id":1444020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1444019#post1444019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing about practitioners is that they aren't able to directly raise their traits above 5, but within the purview of their Principles they can get very scary quite quickly. An Edge-adept is likely to be quite the terrifying fighter, even before you add in Merits like Coat of Scars, for instance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whilst a Knock-adept is able to get just about anywhere, if they just try hard enough, and a Lantern-adept can uncover... pretty much anything, if they put their mind to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1444019#post1444019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was basically my rationale for replacing the Astral, though you could potentially treat the Hours as beings not unlike the Aeons - beings that reside in the Astral but aren't <i>from humanity</i>, or even really from the world like the inhabitants of the Anima Mundi. In fact, you could potentially do something like situate the Wood and the Mansus at the 'heart' of the Astral - a point where the Glory (which, let's face it, has some big Supernal vibes) emanates into a kind of 'tree of life', and all the rest of the Astral is just the muddle that happens outside the Wood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that could actually work! Of course, it\u2019d naturally result in Mages, and other Supernaturals capable of accessing and traversing the Astral, occasionally finding themselves in the outermost borders of the Woods. Naturally, of course, they typically turn tail and make like a road runner that\u2019s being chased by one of its predators at this point our of sheer pants-yellow-soiling terror. Which is perfectly understandable, of course.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1444019#post1444019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eeeeyup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T05:28:11-07:00","id":1444022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerrorCooper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1444020#post1444020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that could actually work! Of course, it\u2019d naturally result in Mages, and other Supernaturals capable of accessing and traversing the Astral, occasionally finding themselves in the outermost borders of the Woods. Naturally, of course, they typically turn tail and make like a road runner that\u2019s being chased by one of its predators at this point our of sheer pants-yellow-soiling terror. Which is perfectly understandable, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, we're talking about mages here. There's a good chance they'd try to get in, be repulsed or lost in the Wood, then come back with a larger group to try and bully their way in. Hubris do be like that sometimes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T05:47:59-07:00","id":1444023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1444022#post1444022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, we're talking about mages here. There's a good chance they'd try to get in, be repulsed or lost in the Wood, then come back with a larger group to try and bully their way in. Hubris do be like that sometimes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which would eventually lead to the entirety of the Mage part of the Supernatural world attempting to lay siege to the Woods, if given sufficient time and not successfully driven off or distracted by something/one else.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I agrees. There\u2019s a reason I\u2019m okay(-ish) with Pride, but absolutely <b><i><u>DESPISE</u></i></b> the self-deluding, self-aggrandisement nature of an unhealthy sense of Arrogance that\u2019s boiled over into outright Hubris. If you wanna know what I consider a \u2018healthy\u2019 sense of Arrogance, just look at Escanor from The Seven Deadly Sins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T07:07:46-07:00","id":1444031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerrorCooper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1444023#post1444023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which would eventually lead to the entirety of the Mage part of the Supernatural world attempting to lay siege to the Woods, if given sufficient time and not successfully driven off or distracted by something/one else.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, that does assume that A) the Hours couldn't drive them off and/or make it impossible for them to find the Mansus in a large enough group to pose any real trouble and/or make them forget the Mansus and B) that mages could come together in large enough numbers to do that in the first place.<br /> <br /> However, I want to revive this sub-topic - does anyone have any particular thoughts on the matter?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1444012#post1444012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I'm debating adding to the thing is the ability to 'subvert' Influences like in the game - that is, take an Influence of one type and transform it into one of another, in a specific 'cycle' (Moth -&gt; Lantern -&gt; Forge -&gt; Edge -&gt; Winter -&gt; Heart -&gt; Grail -&gt; Moth, and any can be subverted to Knock). I'm not sure whether or not I should, though.<br /> <br /> From a functional standpoint subversion exists in the original mostly as a way to counter RNGsus being a bitch sometimes, but in a tabletop game A) you're not at the whim of RNG when it comes to what Influences you find and B) you're going to be playing with others, or at the very least with NPCs, and in those circumstances I was thinking it might be more interesting to have influences be non-fungible, but rather serving as a form of currency between practitioners. Say you happen across a Forge Influence, but you only know Grail magic. You can trade that Influence to a friend or acquaintance for help, or an Influence of theirs and so on.<br /> <br /> The other reason I'm a little reluctant to include it is<br /> <br /> On the other hand, there is still a certain element of 'I might need X while I have Y', or 'I have a source of X but I want Y', and subversion gives you a way to address those problems. Plus, I like the way that the ability to subvert one Influence into another implies that these things aren't totally separate.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T12:42:45-07:00","id":1444054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1444031#post1444031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, that does assume that A) the Hours couldn't drive them off and/or make it impossible for them to find the Mansus in a large enough group to pose any real trouble and/or make them forget the Mansus and B) that mages could come together in large enough numbers to do that in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it is working on both of those assumptions. But, most likely, they're both incorrect.<br /> <br /> As for the subversion, I'm personally not entirely sure on whether to include it or not. Still, I like the 'Influences as Currency between Practitioners' Idea. Mayhaps you could have some sort of minor Ritual or simple(-ish) (set of) roll(s) to govern Subversion? Heck, it could even become part of the currency, in the sense of &quot;The other guy wants Influence X in exchange for Y, but I (only have/can only spare/only have a source of) Z.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T20:53:02-07:00","id":1444128,"title":"","content":"RE: Crossover<br /> <br /> I was actually thinking about making the entire Mansus a weird branch of the <i>Underworld</i>, that bleeds into the Astral and perhaps to others.<br /> <br /> RE: Influence Subversion &amp; and Influence-as-currency<br /> <br /> I like the subversion better. The currency stuff could be still done via Instruments, books, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T02:29:51-07:00","id":1444145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1444128#post1444128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RE: Crossover<br /> <br /> I was actually thinking about making the entire Mansus a weird branch of the <i>Underworld</i>, that bleeds into the Astral and perhaps to others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. I'm a little surprised at that take. Mind if I ask why?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T04:20:19-07:00","id":1444153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1444145#post1444145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. I'm a little surprised at that take. Mind if I ask why?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking about the Hours first led me there. All of them killed or was killed. Death as transformation, and apotheosis. <br /> <br /> Dreams and sleep, the little death. <br /> <br /> The void of Nowhere. <br /> <br /> The importance of cosmic principles and occult resonances, which are embodied in profound memories and cherishable objects, and which act as keys that lead the aspirant deeper into the realm.<br /> <br /> That, and most of the spirits and gods from there being jerks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 04-16-2021, 07:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T04:36:53-07:00","id":1444157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1444153#post1444153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thinking about the Hours first led me there. All of them killed or was killed. Death as transformation, and apotheosis.<br /> <br /> Dreams and sleep, the little death.<br /> <br /> The void of Nowhere.<br /> <br /> The importance of cosmic principles and occult resonances, which are embodied in profound memories and cherishable objects, and which act as keys that lead the aspirant deeper into the realm.<br /> <br /> That, and most of the spirits and gods from there being jerks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. I can kind of see your point, but not all of the Hours died, and a relative minority came from Nowhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T04:49:31-07:00","id":1444163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1444157#post1444157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. I can kind of see your point, but not all of the Hours died, and a relative minority came from Nowhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>AFAIK, the ones who weren\u2019t killed had killed. Or mourns. <br /> The Ocean of Fragments is or is in Nowhere.<br /> <br /> Anyways, it\u2019s not like I\u2019m trying to map out a one-to-one correspondence; all of what I said could be some wacky Krewe\u2019s attempts at trying to make sense of the Mansus and its Hours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T04:22:01-07:00","id":1444320,"title":"","content":"As I'm playing with the mechanics for Influence subversion, I'm looking at the way Influences work in terms of the way they degrade even when held, and I'm worried it's an element of bookkeeping which doesn't really need to be there. What are your opinions on the matter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T07:22:52-07:00","id":1444498,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">I've added rules to the document for the entities which inhabit the Mansus - King Crucible, Maids-in-the-Mirror and the like - added mechanics for Influence subversion and thrown in some stats for a Caligine. I'd appreciate if anyone could look over the mechanics for Eidolons to see if there's any glaring issues there.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T06:46:04-07:00","id":1444644,"title":"","content":"Is the Incarnate Manifestation simply meant to be better than the Materialize Manifestation?<br /> <br /> King Crimson has Forge as Ephemeral!Influence, while Caligine has Bewilderment; both separate from Principles. Maybe eidolons could just have Principles as their Influences, like how Geists have Influence over Keys? Or maybe eidolons don't have Ephemeral!Influence at all, and only have Principles? Like how Goetia don't have Manifestations because they don't naturally manifest on the physical world and they don't need to, perhaps eidolons don't have Ephemeral!Influences over worldly phenomena because they are too closely tied to the Mansus and its abstract cosmic powers.<br /> <br /> Learning new 'standard' Rituals don't cost Experience. Character creation shows Adepts getting three Rituals for free. So these Rituals would be these standard ones? Or can they learn a 'repurposed' Ritual at this stage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T12:55:22-07:00","id":1444704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1444644#post1444644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the Incarnate Manifestation simply meant to be better than the Materialize Manifestation?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the idea, yes. I wanted eidolons to be somewhat more free-acting that normal ephemeral beings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1444644#post1444644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">King Crimson has Forge as Ephemeral!Influence, while Caligine has Bewilderment; both separate from Principles. Maybe eidolons could just have Principles as their Influences, like how Geists have Influence over Keys? Or maybe eidolons don't have Ephemeral!Influence at all, and only have Principles? Like how Goetia don't have Manifestations because they don't naturally manifest on the physical world and they don't need to, perhaps eidolons don't have Ephemeral!Influences over worldly phenomena because they are too closely tied to the Mansus and its abstract cosmic powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea here was that most lesser eidolons have Ephemeral!Influences over more specific things than an entire Principle, while powerful Names like King Crucible or Ezeem get to have direct Influence over a Principle in its entirety.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1444644#post1444644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Learning new 'standard' Rituals don't cost Experience. Character creation shows Adepts getting three Rituals for free. So these Rituals would be these standard ones? Or can they learn a 'repurposed' Ritual at this stage?</div> </div> </div> </div>At character creation, the only difference between a 'standard' ritual and a 'repurposed' ritual is whether or not that ritual is written in the document. So yes, you can take rituals outside the ones detailed if you want to write one up for it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T18:15:52-07:00","id":1444738,"title":"","content":"Ah, makes sense. <br /> <br /> Now I wonder what Ezeem looks like","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T18:26:33-07:00","id":1444739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1444738#post1444738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, makes sense. <br /> <br /> Now I wonder what Ezeem looks like</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll probably do them tomorrow. But, probably terrifyingly good at social nonsense. Definitely got Perfect Lie and Emotional Aura (Desire).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T02:51:40-07:00","id":1445017,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">So, Ezeem didn't get done, but I've added a few new rituals, and a subsystem for Lore, which works somewhat similarly to Arcane Experience in Mage. The idea is that PCs go out and hunt down Scraps, which have tags related to up to three Principles. Five Scraps which all share a tag may be combined into a Lore of that Principle (three Knock scraps, a Knock/Forge scrap and a Knock/Winter scrap could be assembled into a Knock Lore, for instance, but not a Forge or a Winter Lore), which may then be spent to raise your Principles, to buy supernatural Merits or mundane ones appropriate to a given Principle (e.g. you could probably use Lantern Lore to buy Library or Encyclopedic Knowledge, Heart for Allies or Safe Place and so on) or to adapt rituals. Scraps can be traded between players, but Lores can't be.<br /> <br /> Also, I added the possibility of Secret Histories Scraps, Lore and Merits. You don't get Secret Histories Influences or Principle dots, but I liked the idea of at least being able to do stuff with Merits with knowledge of that sort of thing. Any ideas for what those Merits might be are also welcome<br /> <br /> Insight has also been revised so that a dot of Insight only gives you one dot to put into Principles; the rest has to be bought with Lore. I am a little worried that Insight isn't all that impactful besides serving as Supernatural Tolerance and capping Principles, but you're not buying it with Experience or Lore, so it's not a purchase which has to be weighed against anything else.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T04:26:18-07:00","id":1445019,"title":"","content":"Secret Histories Lore... maybe they can be used to purchase <i>any </i>Merit, mortal or Adept, mixed together with Experiences/other Lore,<br /> <br /> Or maybe, by using solely Secret Histories Lore, an Adept can buy any mortal Merit without meeting their prerequisites, similar to Alchemists (Promethean 2E) using Vitriol to buy Merits. Let's justify it by saying the Adept converges with alternate timelines and alternate laws of physics she draws into herself by studying the Secret Histories or something.<br /> <br /> Can Lore be subverted into other Lore like Influences?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 04-21-2021, 07:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T05:21:10-07:00","id":1445025,"title":"","content":"in my opinion you are doing great","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26776-cornelgo","name":"cornelGo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T07:07:48-07:00","id":1445040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1445019#post1445019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secret Histories Lore... maybe they can be used to purchase <i>any </i>Merit, mortal or Adept, mixed together with Experiences/other Lore,<br /> <br /> Or maybe, by using solely Secret Histories Lore, an Adept can buy any mortal Merit without meeting their prerequisites, similar to Alchemists (Promethean 2E) using Vitriol to buy Merits. Let's justify it by saying the Adept converges with alternate timelines and alternate laws of physics she draws into herself by studying the Secret Histories or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not quite how the Histories work, at least by my understanding of them. That said, it probably does have a reasonably broad applicability when it comes to buying mundane Merits, and the idea of it letting you bypass some prereqs is interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1445019#post1445019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Lore be subverted into other Lore like Influences?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. I ended up deciding that this would be the best place to have trade go on between characters - adepts trade in secrets and knowledge, and the place that subverting Lore would go is instead taken up by offering your Knock Scraps to an NPC in exchange for access to <i>Rapt in the King</i> so you can get that last Heart Scrap you need for a Lore and so on. I'm probably going to add a sidebar encouraging STs to be generous with Scraps, especially when PCs are going off on adventures to interesting places and the like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T07:13:14-07:00","id":1445041,"title":"","content":"Oh, I thought the Secret Histories were alternate histories censored by the Hours. Must\u2019ve been mistaken. <br /> <br /> Trading... yeah, trading Scraps and Lore (and maybe Influence?) does feel more like my initial impression of what Cultist Simulator looks like IC, as opposed to trading \u201csolid\u201d stuff like Tools. <br /> <br /> Good work","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T07:16:39-07:00","id":1445042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1443873-practitioners-of-the-invisible-arts-cultist-simulator-in-chronicles?p=1445041#post1445041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I thought the Secret Histories were alternate histories censored by the Hours. Must\u2019ve been mistaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they kind of are, but also kind of not? It seems to be the case that there are alternate pasts, but only one present. Some of that is just normal loss of information, while other aspects seem to be more like... different stories told by the Hours as to why the world is now. And sometimes they decide that something should pass into the Histories rather than remaining in the present - see the destruction of Tower Revek. The Mansus is a constant between all Histories, and beings which ascend to it share at least somewhat in that, but not entirely. <br /> <br /> I don't think you can *travel to* other Histories exactly. You can find places where the remains of Histories intrude upon normal reality, but 'History-hopping' is more like re-writing the past than anything. Like, for instance the Tombs of the Shadowless Kings exist and can be found - but they're not in our History. They were real, and had real power, and existed, and you can touch their bones and suffer their curses, but their History is not ours.<br /> <br /> As with so many things to do with CultSim, it's rather unclear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T08:57:35-07:00","id":1445274,"title":"","content":"So, another thing I'm debating at the moment: Presently, I've got some supernatural Merits which are basically better versions of an ordinary Merit, justified by needing to be an adept to purchase them. Do you think that's alright, or would it be better to make a cheaper version of the Merit consisting of just the supernatural elements, which requires the mundane one as a prerequisite and adds onto it? The example here is Plucking Heartstrings, which is basically Inspiring with some extra Heart magic for turning on the charm offensive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-12T13:51:12-07:00","id":1541985,"title":"","content":"I don't know if this count as necromancy, but I truly love this project. I just have a doubt:<br /> <br /> Influences are a <i>Condition?</i><br /> <br /> I feel a little dumb because I don't know if I'm seeing the implications of this instead of it being just a piece of equipment [specially because people can trade them], why it is a Condition and could I see any example of that Condition in practice?<br /> <br /> Outside of that, I truly like this work, starting to reflavor it for a more interesting way of doing Thaumaturgy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27384-altidiya","name":"altidiya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-11T09:42:50-07:00","id":1553750,"title":"","content":"Just logging in to say that I was thinking about this homebrew again. It's a really interesting and solid work, that feels like it meets it's design goals elegantly and well. Thanks for making it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}